{title: Oh! Susanna}
{artist: Stephen Foster}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I [G]come from Alabama with my [D]banjo on my knee
I'm [G]goin' to Louisiana, my [D]true love for to [G]see
It [G]rained all night the day I left, the [D]weather it was dry
The [G]sun so hot I froze to death, Su-[D]sanna, don't you [G]cry
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Oh! Su-[G]sanna, oh [D]don't you cry for me
For I [G]come from Alabama with my [D]banjo on my [G]knee
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I [G]had a dream the other night, when [D]everything was still
I [G]thought I saw Susanna a-[D]coming down the [G]hill
The [G]buckwheat cake was in her mouth, the [D]tear was in her eye
Says [G]I, I'm coming from the south, Su-[D]sanna, don't you [G]cry
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
